2025-07-16 20:12:04 | INFO     | api.endpoints.qa:generate_sse:637 - [SOURCES_SAVE_DEBUG] - knowledge_sources_collected内容: [{'id': '12b6483b-e844-4242-a315-6d9e74564d12', 'content': '问题: 文中提到的摩尔比Si/Al和Na/Si是如何计算的，这些摩尔比在地聚合物反应中扮演什么角色？\n答案: A：摩尔比Si/Al和Na/Si是根据前驱体材料（飞灰、赤泥、硅灰）和碱性活化剂（氢氧化钠、硅酸钠）的初始化学成分计算得出的。这些摩尔比是地聚合物反应现象的关键参数。Si/Al比决定了地聚合物凝胶的硅铝酸盐骨架组成，影响结构的聚合程度、致密性和稳定性。Na/Si比则反映了体系的碱性强度和钠离子的含量，钠离子在地聚合物化反应中作为电荷平衡剂，同时其浓度会影响硅铝酸盐的溶解速率和凝胶的形成过程。这些比值对最终产品的力学性能和微观结构有决定性影响。', 'title': 'QA: 文中提到的摩尔比Si/Al和Na/Si是如何计算的，这些摩尔比在地聚合物反应中扮演什么角色？...', 'score': 0.9058838599999998, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': 'e1e864c1-4358-4c21-b77e-208d81a9eef1', 'content': '问题: 比较碱激活剂SiO₂/Na₂O摩尔比为0.96（M-0.96）、1.28（M-1.28）和1.91（M-1.91）的地聚合物浆体在固化28天后的抗压强度和抗折强度，并分析其性能差异的成因。\n答案: 固化28天后，M-0.96和M-1.28浆体的抗压强度分别达到约47.1 MPa和46.4 MPa，而M-1.91浆体的抗压强度则显著较低，表明其性能较差。同样，M-0.96和M-1.28的抗折强度分别为18.4 MPa和16.8 MPa，远高于M-1.91。这种差异主要是由于SiO₂/Na₂O摩尔比过高（如1.91）会降低碱溶液的碱度，导致从矿渣和粉煤灰中溶解的Si和Al离子不足，从而抑制了地聚合物反应的程度，形成了孔隙率更高（M-1.91的孔隙率为42.3%）且结构致密性更差的产物，最终降低了机械强度。', 'title': 'QA: 比较碱激活剂SiO₂/Na₂O摩尔比为0.96（M-0.96）、1.28（M-1.28）和1.91（...', 'score': 0.85935752, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '34d84a04-9c06-4243-bd9a-b8b97af88969', 'content': 'the temperature range of ambient to ${800}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , with a heating rate of ${10}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ per minute and under an inert atmosphere of nitrogen. The samples (ambient cured for 28 days) were ground to a fine powder so as to ensure the thermal equilibrium (Fig. 2). ![01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg](images/01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratios of alkaline solution\n## Results and discussion\n## Workability of geopolymer concrete mixes\nThe workability of geopolymer concrete was ensured in accordance with the IS 1199: 1959 in a manner similar to that of OPC concrete. The slump values of all the mixes are mentioned in Fig. 2. From the results, it can be seen that the mix with the ratio of 0.5 had the highest slump of ${250}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ , while the mix with the ratio of 2.5 had the lowest slump of ${215}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ . It is also observed from Table 2 that with an increase in the ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio, the ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ increased and made the mix more viscous, and due to this the slump decreased. From this, it is evident that the alkaline solution in the mix plays a dominant role in the workability of fresh geopolymer concrete. In the present study, with an increase in the ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 0.5 to 2.5, the slump of the ternary blended geo-polymer concrete decreased from 250 to ${215}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ . Similar observations were reported by Nath and Sarker [13], i.e., with an increase in ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 1.5 to 2.5, the slump values also reduced from 245 to 230 . Similar kind of results has been reported by Nath et al. [13].\n## Compressive strength and the importance of kinetic ratios in geopolymer concrete', 'title': '', 'score': 0.24, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': 'the temperature range of ambient to ${800}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ , with a heating rate of ${10}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ per minute and under an inert atmosphere of nitrogen. The samples (ambient cured for 28 days) were ground to a fine powder so as to ensure the thermal equilibrium (Fig. 2). ![01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg](images/01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratios of alkaline solution\\n## Results and discussion\\n## Workability of geopolymer concrete mixes\\nThe workability of geopolymer concrete was ensured in accordance with the IS 1199: 1959 in a manner similar to that of OPC concrete. The slump values of all the mixes are mentioned in Fig. 2. From the results, it can be seen that the mix with the ratio of 0.5 had the highest slump of ${250}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ , while the mix with the ratio of 2.5 had the lowest slump of ${215}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ . It is also observed from Table 2 that with an increase in the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio, the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ increased and made the mix more viscous, and due to this the slump decreased. From this, it is evident that the alkaline solution in the mix plays a dominant role in the workability of fresh geopolymer concrete. In the present study, with an increase in the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 0.5 to 2.5, the slump of the ternary blended geo-polymer concrete decreased from 250 to ${215}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ . Similar observations were reported by Nath and Sarker [13], i.e., with an increase in ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 1.5 to 2.5, the slump values also reduced from 245 to 230 . Similar kind of results has been reported by Nath et al. [13].\\n## Compressive strength and the importance of kinetic ratios in geopolymer concrete', 'domain_text': 'the temperature range of ambient to ${800}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ , with a heating rate of ${10}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ per minute and under an inert atmosphere of nitrogen. The samples (ambient cured for 28 days) were ground to a fine powder so as to ensure the thermal equilibrium (Fig. 2). ![01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg](images/01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratios of alkaline solution\\n## Results and discussion\\n## Workability of geopolymer concrete mixes\\nThe workability of geopolymer concrete was ensured in accordance with the IS 1199: 1959 in a manner similar to that of OPC concrete. The slump values of all the mixes are mentioned in Fig. 2. From the results, it can be seen that the mix with the ratio of 0.5 had the highest slump of ${250}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ , while the mix with the ratio of 2.5 had the lowest slump of ${215}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ . It is also observed from Table 2 that with an increase in the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio, the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ increased and made the mix more viscous, and due to this the slump decreased. From this, it is evident that the a', 'original_tokens': 610, 'general_tokens': 610, 'domain_tokens': 458, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{<mark>NaOH</mark>', 'Similar observations were reported by <mark>Nath</mark> and Sarker [13], i.e., with an increase in ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{<mark>NaOH</mark>}}$', 'Similar kind of results has been reported by <mark>Nath</mark> et al. [13].\n## Compressive strength and the importance of kinetic ratios in geopolymer concrete']}, 'adopted': True}, {'id': '12b6483b-e844-4242-a315-6d9e74564d12', 'content': '问题: 文中提到的摩尔比Si/Al和Na/Si是如何计算的，这些摩尔比在地聚合物反应中扮演什么角色？\n答案: A：摩尔比Si/Al和Na/Si是根据前驱体材料（飞灰、赤泥、硅灰）和碱性活化剂（氢氧化钠、硅酸钠）的初始化学成分计算得出的。这些摩尔比是地聚合物反应现象的关键参数。Si/Al比决定了地聚合物凝胶的硅铝酸盐骨架组成，影响结构的聚合程度、致密性和稳定性。Na/Si比则反映了体系的碱性强度和钠离子的含量，钠离子在地聚合物化反应中作为电荷平衡剂，同时其浓度会影响硅铝酸盐的溶解速率和凝胶的形成过程。这些比值对最终产品的力学性能和微观结构有决定性影响。', 'title': 'QA: 文中提到的摩尔比Si/Al和Na/Si是如何计算的，这些摩尔比在地聚合物反应中扮演什么角色？...', 'score': 0.9058838599999998, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': 'e1e864c1-4358-4c21-b77e-208d81a9eef1', 'content': '问题: 比较碱激活剂SiO₂/Na₂O摩尔比为0.96（M-0.96）、1.28（M-1.28）和1.91（M-1.91）的地聚合物浆体在固化28天后的抗压强度和抗折强度，并分析其性能差异的成因。\n答案: 固化28天后，M-0.96和M-1.28浆体的抗压强度分别达到约47.1 MPa和46.4 MPa，而M-1.91浆体的抗压强度则显著较低，表明其性能较差。同样，M-0.96和M-1.28的抗折强度分别为18.4 MPa和16.8 MPa，远高于M-1.91。这种差异主要是由于SiO₂/Na₂O摩尔比过高（如1.91）会降低碱溶液的碱度，导致从矿渣和粉煤灰中溶解的Si和Al离子不足，从而抑制了地聚合物反应的程度，形成了孔隙率更高（M-1.91的孔隙率为42.3%）且结构致密性更差的产物，最终降低了机械强度。', 'title': 'QA: 比较碱激活剂SiO₂/Na₂O摩尔比为0.96（M-0.96）、1.28（M-1.28）和1.91（...', 'score': 0.85935752, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '34d84a04-9c06-4243-bd9a-b8b97af88969', 'content': 'the temperature range of ambient to ${800}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , with a heating rate of ${10}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ per minute and under an inert atmosphere of nitrogen. The samples (ambient cured for 28 days) were ground to a fine powder so as to ensure the thermal equilibrium (Fig. 2). ![01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg](images/01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratios of alkaline solution\n## Results and discussion\n## Workability of geopolymer concrete mixes\nThe workability of geopolymer concrete was ensured in accordance with the IS 1199: 1959 in a manner similar to that of OPC concrete. The slump values of all the mixes are mentioned in Fig. 2. From the results, it can be seen that the mix with the ratio of 0.5 had the highest slump of ${250}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ , while the mix with the ratio of 2.5 had the lowest slump of ${215}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ . It is also observed from Table 2 that with an increase in the ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio, the ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ increased and made the mix more viscous, and due to this the slump decreased. From this, it is evident that the alkaline solution in the mix plays a dominant role in the workability of fresh geopolymer concrete. In the present study, with an increase in the ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 0.5 to 2.5, the slump of the ternary blended geo-polymer concrete decreased from 250 to ${215}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ . Similar observations were reported by Nath and Sarker [13], i.e., with an increase in ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 1.5 to 2.5, the slump values also reduced from 245 to 230 . Similar kind of results has been reported by Nath et al. [13].\n## Compressive strength and the importance of kinetic ratios in geopolymer concrete', 'title': '', 'score': 0.24, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': 'the temperature range of ambient to ${800}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ , with a heating rate of ${10}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ per minute and under an inert atmosphere of nitrogen. The samples (ambient cured for 28 days) were ground to a fine powder so as to ensure the thermal equilibrium (Fig. 2). ![01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg](images/01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratios of alkaline solution\\n## Results and discussion\\n## Workability of geopolymer concrete mixes\\nThe workability of geopolymer concrete was ensured in accordance with the IS 1199: 1959 in a manner similar to that of OPC concrete. The slump values of all the mixes are mentioned in Fig. 2. From the results, it can be seen that the mix with the ratio of 0.5 had the highest slump of ${250}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ , while the mix with the ratio of 2.5 had the lowest slump of ${215}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ . It is also observed from Table 2 that with an increase in the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio, the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ increased and made the mix more viscous, and due to this the slump decreased. From this, it is evident that the alkaline solution in the mix plays a dominant role in the workability of fresh geopolymer concrete. In the present study, with an increase in the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 0.5 to 2.5, the slump of the ternary blended geo-polymer concrete decreased from 250 to ${215}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ . Similar observations were reported by Nath and Sarker [13], i.e., with an increase in ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio from 1.5 to 2.5, the slump values also reduced from 245 to 230 . Similar kind of results has been reported by Nath et al. [13].\\n## Compressive strength and the importance of kinetic ratios in geopolymer concrete', 'domain_text': 'the temperature range of ambient to ${800}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ , with a heating rate of ${10}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ per minute and under an inert atmosphere of nitrogen. The samples (ambient cured for 28 days) were ground to a fine powder so as to ensure the thermal equilibrium (Fig. 2). ![01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg](images/01974571-ed5b-7d60-8f6d-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratios of alkaline solution\\n## Results and discussion\\n## Workability of geopolymer concrete mixes\\nThe workability of geopolymer concrete was ensured in accordance with the IS 1199: 1959 in a manner similar to that of OPC concrete. The slump values of all the mixes are mentioned in Fig. 2. From the results, it can be seen that the mix with the ratio of 0.5 had the highest slump of ${250}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ , while the mix with the ratio of 2.5 had the lowest slump of ${215}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;{mm}}$ . It is also observed from Table 2 that with an increase in the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ ratio, the ${\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ increased and made the mix more viscous, and due to this the slump decreased. From this, it is evident that the a', 'original_tokens': 610, 'general_tokens': 610, 'domain_tokens': 458, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['-0b931f20327f_4_901_1485_707_537_0.jpg) Fig. 2 Workability of geopolymer concrete different ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{<mark>NaOH</mark>', 'Similar observations were reported by <mark>Nath</mark> and Sarker [13], i.e., with an increase in ${\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{3}$ -to- $\\mathrm{{<mark>NaOH</mark>}}$', 'Similar kind of results has been reported by <mark>Nath</mark> et al. [13].\n## Compressive strength and the importance of kinetic ratios in geopolymer concrete']}, 'adopted': True}, {'id': '1e967ebd-5942-463c-90c3-43c8cbabcdef', 'content': '问题: 对金尾矿原材料进行颗粒级配分析显示，其平均粒径（D50）为0.035 mm，细颗粒含量达63.88%。这些物理特性对制备地聚合物材料有何影响？\n答案: A：金尾矿原材料的平均粒径D50为0.035 mm，细颗粒含量高达63.88%，统一系数Cu为17.67，表明其颗粒较细且级配范围较广。这些特性有利于地聚合物的制备，因为细颗粒提供了更大的比表面积，有助于与碱性活化剂充分接触并促进硅铝酸盐的溶解和反应。较高的细颗粒含量也意味着材料具有更好的填充性，有助于形成更致密的地聚合物结构，从而提高材料的强度和稳定性。根据USCS分类，其被归类为含砂砾质粉土（CL-ML），具有低塑性，这使得其更适合作为地聚合物的原料。', 'title': 'QA: 对金尾矿原材料进行颗粒级配分析显示，其平均粒径（D50）为0.035 mm，细颗粒含量达63.88%...', 'score': 0.8733178999999999, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '3e13b341-8e2e-46ea-9993-e98e3c7e7f04', 'content': '问题: 金尾矿原材料的X射线衍射（XRD）分析显示，石英（Quartz）是主要的矿物组分，含量约为54.2%。这一发现对地聚合物的反应性和最终性能有何影响？\n答案: A：金尾矿原材料中石英含量高达54.2%，是主要的矿物组分。根据Davidovits的研究，石英的晶体形式在地聚合物技术中反应性较低。这意味着在碱激活过程中，大部分石英可能保持未反应状态，充当骨料而非主要的胶凝组分来源。虽然石英本身的反应性不高，但其存在为地聚合物提供了骨架支撑，有助于提高材料的稳定性和抗压强度。然而，过高的惰性石英含量可能限制地聚合物凝胶的形成量，从而影响材料的最终胶凝性能和重金属固化效果。', 'title': 'QA: 金尾矿原材料的X射线衍射（XRD）分析显示，石英（Quartz）是主要的矿物组分，含量约为54.2%...', 'score': 0.82519437, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '1e967ebd-5942-463c-90c3-43c8cbabcdef', 'content': '问题: 对金尾矿原材料进行颗粒级配分析显示，其平均粒径（D50）为0.035 mm，细颗粒含量达63.88%。这些物理特性对制备地聚合物材料有何影响？\n答案: A：金尾矿原材料的平均粒径D50为0.035 mm，细颗粒含量高达63.88%，统一系数Cu为17.67，表明其颗粒较细且级配范围较广。这些特性有利于地聚合物的制备，因为细颗粒提供了更大的比表面积，有助于与碱性活化剂充分接触并促进硅铝酸盐的溶解和反应。较高的细颗粒含量也意味着材料具有更好的填充性，有助于形成更致密的地聚合物结构，从而提高材料的强度和稳定性。根据USCS分类，其被归类为含砂砾质粉土（CL-ML），具有低塑性，这使得其更适合作为地聚合物的原料。', 'title': 'QA: 对金尾矿原材料进行颗粒级配分析显示，其平均粒径（D50）为0.035 mm，细颗粒含量达63.88%...', 'score': 0.8733178999999999, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '3e13b341-8e2e-46ea-9993-e98e3c7e7f04', 'content': '问题: 金尾矿原材料的X射线衍射（XRD）分析显示，石英（Quartz）是主要的矿物组分，含量约为54.2%。这一发现对地聚合物的反应性和最终性能有何影响？\n答案: A：金尾矿原材料中石英含量高达54.2%，是主要的矿物组分。根据Davidovits的研究，石英的晶体形式在地聚合物技术中反应性较低。这意味着在碱激活过程中，大部分石英可能保持未反应状态，充当骨料而非主要的胶凝组分来源。虽然石英本身的反应性不高，但其存在为地聚合物提供了骨架支撑，有助于提高材料的稳定性和抗压强度。然而，过高的惰性石英含量可能限制地聚合物凝胶的形成量，从而影响材料的最终胶凝性能和重金属固化效果。', 'title': 'QA: 金尾矿原材料的X射线衍射（XRD）分析显示，石英（Quartz）是主要的矿物组分，含量约为54.2%...', 'score': 0.82519437, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}]
